<h1>Week 19</h1>

<p><strong>From:</strong> Kayla</p>
<p><strong>Artist:</strong> Foxing</p>
<p><strong>Album:</strong> <em>Draw Down the Moon</em></p>

<p>Lana,</p>

<p>
My pick for you this week is <em>Draw Down the Moon</em> by Foxing. This is their fourth album, and for some reason this record always makes me think about you.
</p>

<p>
I honestly think this is an amazing album. I love almost every song on it except <em>Bialystok</em>.
</p>

<p>
“Where the Lightning Strikes” reminds me so much of <em>Knights of Cydonia</em> by Muse. It has that same kind of dramatic, cinematic energy that builds and pulls you in.
</p>

<p>
“Speak with the Dead” always makes me think of Chloe, especially the last lines of the song.
</p>

<p>
Since this is their fourth record, I’m really interested to hear your reaction to how they sound now and whether you feel like it’s a big departure from their first album.
</p>

<p>
I hope you like it.
</p>

<p>
Kayla
</p>

